          "unit_id": "expressing_opinions",
          "title": "The First Meeting",
          "description": "Defiende tu opinión con conectores de contraste: although, despite, however, whereas.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "opinion_linkers",
              "title": "Linkers of contrast",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The first meeting",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Although I like the colours, the homepage feels too simple."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I understand. However, our research shows that guests want to book quickly."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Despite that, I think luxury needs more photos and more text."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "If I may, Lucía has hit the nail on the head. Simple sells."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Well, it seems we don't see eye to eye on this."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "In spite of being simple, the design is much faster. Your current site takes ten seconds to load, whereas this one takes two."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Two seconds? That's interesting. Helen, what's your opinion? You can't sit on the fence forever."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Helen",
                        "text": "I'm not sitting on the fence. I agree with Lucía, even though you're paying the bill."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Ha! I like honesty. Nevertheless, I need to see two versions."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "That's fair. We'll prepare a simple version and a richer one."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Mark",
                        "text": "Deal."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "November. Mark Reed is in Bristol for the first meeting with Harbour Studio. He isn't sure about Lucía's designs."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
                    "instructions": "Fíjate en el diálogo y responde.",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "question": "\"Although I like the colours, the homepage feels too simple.\" After although we use…",
                        "options": [
                          "subject + verb",
                          "a noun only"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"Despite that…\" After despite we use…",
                        "options": [
                          "a noun or -ing",
                          "subject + verb"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"However, our research shows…\" However usually…",
                        "options": [
                          "starts a new sentence, with a comma",
                          "joins two clauses without punctuation"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"We don't see eye to eye.\" means…",
                        "options": [
                          "no estamos de acuerdo",
                          "nos miramos a los ojos"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Linkers of contrast",
                    "explanation": "Para contraponer ideas:\n• although / even though + sujeto + verbo: Although I like the colours, it feels too simple. (Even though es más enfático.)\n• despite / in spite of + nombre o -ing: In spite of being simple, it's faster. Despite that, …\n• however / nevertheless empiezan una frase nueva y van seguidos de coma: However, our research shows… (Nevertheless es más formal.)\n• whereas contrasta dos hechos: Your site takes ten seconds, whereas this one takes two.\n\nPara opinar en una reunión: If I may…, I agree with…, I'm not sure about…, We don't see eye to eye, Don't sit on the fence.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Conector",
                        "Va seguido de",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "although / even though",
                          "sujeto + verbo",
                          "Although I like the colours, it feels too simple."
                        ],
                        [
                          "despite / in spite of",
                          "nombre o -ing",
                          "In spite of being simple, it's faster."
                        ],
                        [
                          "however",
                          "nueva frase + coma",
                          "However, our research shows…"
                        ],
                        [
                          "nevertheless",
                          "nueva frase (más formal)",
                          "Nevertheless, I need two versions."
                        ],
                        [
                          "whereas",
                          "contraste entre dos hechos",
                          "Yours takes ten seconds, whereas ours takes two."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Although I like the colours, the homepage feels too simple.",
                      "Despite that, I think luxury needs more photos.",
                      "I agree with Lucía, even though you're paying the bill.",
                      "Nevertheless, I need to see two versions."
                    ]
                  }
                },
